CHECK:ARCH_INCLUDE_LINUX: Consider using #include <linux/thread_info.h> instead of <asm/thread_info.h>
#190: FILE: arch/arm64/kernel/syscall.c:9:
+#include <asm/thread_info.h>

Whenever asm/file.h is included and linux/file.h exists, a
conversion can be made when linux/file.h includes asm/file.h.
However this is not always the case (See signal.h).
This message type is emitted only for includes from arch/.

WARNING:AVOID_EXTERNS: externs should be avoided in .c files
#217: FILE: arch/arm64/kernel/syscall.c:42:
+void syscall_trace_exit(struct pt_regs *regs);

Function prototypes don't need to be declared extern in .h
files.  It's assumed by the compiler and is unnecessary.

WARNING:ENOSYS: ENOSYS means 'invalid syscall nr' and nothing else
#233: FILE: arch/arm64/kernel/syscall.c:58:
+			regs->regs[0] = -ENOSYS;

ENOSYS means that a nonexistent system call was called.
Earlier, it was wrongly used for things like invalid operations on
otherwise valid syscalls.  This should be avoided in new code.

See: https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/5eb299021dec23c1a48fa7d9f2c8b794e967766d.1408730669.git.luto@amacapital.net/

